{"id":"119-sjres-71","label":"S.J.Res. 71","congress":119,"title":"A joint resolution terminating the national emergency declared with respect to energy.","latestVote":"2025-10-08","rollIds":["Senate:1:554"],"hasMetadata":true,"chambers":["Senate"],"congressUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-joint-resolution/71","metadataUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/sjres/BILLSTATUS-119sjres71.xml","metadata":{"title":"A joint resolution terminating the national emergency declared with respect to energy.","introduced":"2025-07-31","latestAction":"Failed of passage in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 47 - 51. Record Vote Number: 554.","latestActionDate":"2025-10-08","policyArea":"Emergency Management","subjects":["Administrative law and regulatory procedures","Alternative and renewable resources","Building construction","Coal","Energy storage, supplies, demand","Licensing and registrations","Mining","Oil and gas"],"sponsors":["Sen. Kaine, Tim [D-VA]"],"cosponsors":["Sen. Heinrich, Martin [D-NM]","Sen. Whitehouse, Sheldon [D-RI]","Sen. Booker, Cory A. [D-NJ]","Sen. Sanders, Bernard [I-VT]","Sen. Reed, Jack [D-RI]","Sen. Van Hollen, Chris [D-MD]","Sen. Markey, Edward J. [D-MA]","Sen. Shaheen, Jeanne [D-NH]"],"committees":["Energy and Natural Resources Committee"],"laws":[],"committeeReports":[],"costEstimates":[],"relatedBills":[{"title":"A joint resolution terminating the national emergency declared with respect to energy.","relationship":"Identical bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-joint-resolution/10"}],"textVersions":[{"date":"2025-07-31","stage":"Introduced in Senate","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119sjres71is/xml/BILLS-119sjres71is.xml"}],"summaries":[{"date":"2025-07-31","stage":"Introduced in Senate","text":"This joint resolution terminates the national emergency relating to energy declared by the President on January 20, 2025, in Executive Order 14156. \n\nThe executive order states that the supply of and infrastructure for energy in the United States is insufficient to meet the country's needs. It defines energy as crude oil, natural gas, lease condensates, natural gas liquids, refined petroleum products, uranium, coal, biofuels, geothermal heat, the kinetic movement of flowing water, and critical minerals. \n\nThe executive order directs the heads of executive departments and agencies to use available emergency and other authorities to take certain actions to address this topic, including approving development of domestic energy resources, expediting the completion of authorized energy infrastructure (particularly in the Northeast, West Coast, and Alaska), and pursuing the use of emergency permitting provisions under certain environmental regulations.\n\nThe executive order also directs the Department of Defense to conduct an assessment of its ability to acquire and transport energy resources (particularly in the Northeast and West Coast), and invokes emergency military construction authority to address any vulnerabilities identified in the assessment."}],"actions":[{"date":"2025-10-08","text":"Failed of passage in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 47 - 51. Record Vote Number: 554."},{"date":"2025-10-08","text":"Failed of passage/not agreed to in Senate: Failed of passage in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 47 - 51. Record Vote Number: 554."},{"date":"2025-10-08","text":"Measure laid before Senate by unanimous consent. (consideration: CR S7016-7030; text: CR S7016)"},{"date":"2025-10-08","text":"Senate Committee on Energy and Natural Resources discharged by Unanimous Consent."},{"date":"2025-10-08","text":"Senate Committee on Energy and Natural Resources discharged by Unanimous Consent."},{"date":"2025-07-31","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Energy and Natural Resources."},{"date":"2025-07-31","text":"Introduced in Senate"}]},"votes":[{"chamber":"Senate","congress":119,"session":1,"roll":554,"date":"2025-10-08","time":"07:05 PM","question":"On the 